 "notes": "Claude first pass. Baseline 158-162 early (borderline tachycardia) stepping down to ~130-140 after -28. Isolated deep narrow variables for the first hour, then from -19 a relentless train of deep wide troughs (nadirs 60-80) with rebounds to 160-190 between them; zoom checks confirm the detector windows cover each trough - no misses, no false positives. All 26 events typed variable on morphology. Toco dead (flat 0-8) after -7: d23-d26 carry the UC flag, as do d15 (toco 0-4). Striking mismatch between this tracing and pH 7.24 - the 160-190 rebounds in the second stage could be maternal-HR capture; reviewer please eyeball d17-d26. Sub-threshold wobble dips (-52.9, -3.4) not annotated.",
